  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the whole game in `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it or `vite build`, so it hasn't been tested in a browser.\n\n- **Scene:** The scene is built with `createAuraApp` on the existing `#app` canvas. It has a 3×3 grid of pedestals, each with a dark hole, over a dark floor with bloom. Glowing lanterns and purple bombs rise out of the holes. The camera is a fixed perspective one.\n- **Picking:** I wrote my own picking code instead of using the engine's raycast helpers. It assumes the engine's `fov` is the vertical field of view in degrees, which the engine source suggests but I didn't confirm in a render. If that is wrong, clicks and hover would land on the wrong cells.\n- **Rules:**\n  - A lantern pop gives +10 and a burst of sparks.\n  - An empty or lowered cell costs 5 (never below 0) and flashes red.\n  - A bomb ends the run as `lost`.\n  - The round lasts 45 seconds and is `won` at 150 points or more.\n  - A lantern's visible time shortens as the score rises, and a second target can appear once the score reaches 60.\n  - A lantern that drops unpopped costs nothing.\n- **Random generator:** The generator is seeded (default 20240611, or `?seed=N` in the URL). Each spawn draws the same three values in the same order, so a seed repeats its spawn order.\n- **Controls:** A Start button or Enter begins the first round. R or the Restart button on the end overlay starts a new one. A cell highlights on hover while the game is playing.\n- **HUD and state:** A DOM HUD below the canvas shows score, time left and status, with a short \"+10\" or \"-5\" message. The overlay on round end is positioned over the canvas. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is updated every frame, and `window.__TASK_READY__` is set on the first frame of my own `requestAnimationFrame` loop. That loop drives the game logic while the engine does the rendering.\n\nIf the engine fails to initialise, `__TASK_READY__` is never set. The error goes to `console.error` and `document.body.dataset.error`.\n\n",
